Playwright Login Automation Tests

This project contains automated UI tests for the login page on the Expand Testing practice website.

The tests are written in Python using Playwright and Pytest.
-------------------------------------------------------------------
Test coverage

The project covers the main login scenarios:

- successful login with valid credentials
- login by pressing the Enter key
- keyboard navigation using Tab
- successful login after a failed attempt
- invalid username
- invalid password
- empty credentials
- empty username or password
- whitespace-only values
- credentials with incorrect letter case
- username with leading and trailing spaces
- long username
- username with special characters

Negative scenarios are implemented using `pytest.mark.parametrize` to avoid duplicated test code.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Project approach

- A session-scoped fixture starts the browser once for the test session.
- A new browser page is created for every test to keep tests isolated.
- Repeated login actions are moved to a reusable helper function.
- Playwright assertions are used to verify URLs, messages, element visibility, and keyboard focus.
- Tests run in Chromium in headless mode.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Installation

```bash
pip install pytest playwright pytest-html
playwright install chromium
